=== Text #10 ===
> After the martyrdom of[ St].[ Bon]iface, Vergilius was made Bishop of[ Sal]z[burg] (766 or 767) and laboured successfully for the upbuilding of his diocese as well as for the spread of the Faith in neighbouring heat[hen] countries,[ especially] in Carinth[ia]. He died at[ Sal]z[burg], 27 November, 7[89]. In 1233 he was canonized by[ Gregory IX]. His doctrine that[ the] earth is a sphere was derived from the teaching[ of] ancient geographers[, and] his belief in the existence of the antipodes was probably influenced by the accounts[ which the] ancient[ Irish voy]agers gave of their journeys.[ This], at[ least], is the opinion[ of] Rett[berg ("K]irchengesch.[ De]utsch[lands]", II, 236).[][][][][][]


